    <DataNode elementId="Mannosyl5-N-Glycans" textLabel="Man₅(GlcNAc)₂-[protein] (isomer 5A₁,₂)" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="MNXM148697" dataSource="MetaNetX" />
      <Graphics centerX="200" centerY="500" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="PMN, zhang, SRI, caspi">This is one of four possible isomers of Man&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;GlcNAc&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; chains. It is the turning point between the processing phase of high-mannose &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-glycans and the synthesis phase of complex and hybrid &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-glycans. It is the substrate for the first &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-acetylglucosaminyltransferase that is involved in the synthesis of the latter, |FRAME: EC-2.4.1.101|. The nomenclature used to identify high mannose glycans has not been standardized. Several earlier systems were insufficient to describe all possible isomers |CITS: [7954510][17719235][17685584]|. The nomenclature used here is that proposed by Prien et al |CITS: [19181540]|, which can represent all processing isomers. According to this nomenclature, the other three Man&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;GlcNAc&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt; isomers are named isomer 5A&lt;sub&gt;2,3&lt;/sub&gt;, isomer 5A&lt;sub&gt;1,3&lt;/sub&gt;, and isomer 5A&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;B&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;. According to the nomenclature used for hybrid and complex &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-glycans, this compound is known simply as M&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt; |CITS: [24178944]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="Mannosyl5-N-Glycans" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Metanetx" value="MNXM148697" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="an [&amp;alpha;-D-Man-(1&amp;rarr;3)-{&amp;alpha;-D-Man-(1&amp;rarr;3)-[&amp;alpha;-D-Man-(1&amp;rarr;6)]-&amp;alpha;-D-Man-(1&amp;rarr;6)}-&amp;beta;-D-Man-(1&amp;rarr;4)-&amp;beta;-D-GlcNAc-(1&amp;rarr;4)-&amp;beta;-D-GlcNAc]-&lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-Asn-[protein]" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="a [(mannosyl)&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt;(&lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-acetylglucosaminyl)&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;]-L-asparginyl-[protein] (isomer 5A&lt;sub&gt;1,2&lt;/sub&gt;)" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="M&lt;sub&gt;5&lt;/sub&gt; &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-glycan" />
